    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118">

                <pb facs="0194" n="182" xml:id="pg182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">857.0011/85: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Greene</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-08-13T09:00:00+01:00">August 13, 1940—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 13—7:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>826. My 816, Aug. 9, 4 p.m.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d118-f1"/> Following the
                    Norwegian Crown Princess’ departure from Stockholm yesterday the Norwegian
                    Legation gave to the press the following statement which was broadcast by
                    Swedish radio last evening and published in all newspapers this morning: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Crown Princess Martha of Norway and her three children, the Princesses
                            Ragnhild and Astrid and Prince Harald, will leave for the United States
                            in the next few days to visit President Roosevelt. The President has
                            sent a personal invitation to Crown Princess Martha to visit him with
                            her children, and the departure will be by an American ship from
                                Petsamo.”<anchor n="40" xml:id="d118-f2"/>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Greene</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d118-f1" n="39" xml:id="d118-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d118-f2" n="40" xml:id="d118-f2-content">
                <p>In undated telegram received August 16, 5:43 a.m., from the Department’s
                    representative on the return voyage of the <hi rendition="#italic">American
                        Legion</hi>, it was stated that Crown Princess Martha and suite arrived on
                    board the <hi rendition="#italic">American Legion</hi> at 8 p.m. on August 15
                    (340.1115A/1365).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
